racter is not supposed to move at all, but instead the red blocks are supposed to be moved into the hole using some other mechanic? What if SPACE is used to \"shoot\" or \"push\" red blocks?\nOr what if the goal is simply to have the character in a specific orientation at a specific location? Let me check if there's a target position indicated somewhere.\nActually, I just realized something. The green shape has a U-shape with a hole. The character also has a U-shape. What if the goal is to fit the character INTO the green shape's hole, like a puzzle piece? The character would need to be oriented correctly and positioned at the hole.\nLet me check the hole's dimensions and the character's dimensions to see if they match.\nActually, let me try a completely different approach. Let me look at the initial state more carefully and see if there's a pattern or target configuration indicated.\nWait, I just noticed something in the current image. The character is facing left, with red blocks to its left. The green shape is to the right. What if I need to rotate the character to face the green shape (right) and then move into it?\nLet me try rotating to face right and then moving right into the green shape.", "kind": "reasoning", "inContext": false}, {"label": "TOOL CALL: python", "content": "<tool_call>\n<function=python>\n<parameter=code>\n# Let me check current state and try rotating to face right, then moving into the green shape\nseg = current_frame.segmentation\nnodes = seg['nodes']\nfor n in nodes:\n    b = n['boundary']\n    rows = [p[0] for p in b]\n    cols = [p[1] for p in b]\n    if n['pixels'] > 5:\n        print(f\"  color={n['color']}, pixels={n['pixels']}, bbox=({min(rows)},{min(cols)})-({max(rows)},{max(cols)})\")\n\n# Try rotating to face right (need 2 SPACE presses to go from left to right)\naction(['SPACE', 'SPACE'])\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "kind": "tool", "inContext": true}, {"label": "TOOL RESULT: python", "content": "color=S, pixels=37